{"id":"nchi-54ffe9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drag a face onto any window to give an agent context","description":"Dropping a face on a window gives an agent **context**. It doesn't control the app. The drop point identifies the window, and Accessibility (the permission Nocchi already asks for to raise the exact window) reads what's in it.\n\n**Drag sources and what the drop means**\n\n| Face you drag | Drop means |\n|---|---|\n| Focus card's big face | Context for the main agent: opens the composer to it with a context chip |\n| A chip's small face | The same, for that agent |\n| The new-chat composer's face | Start a new agent with this context; the folder switches to the project if the context has a path |\n\nNo dragging from the collapsed notch: hovering opens it within about 90 ms.\n\n**Constraints**\n- Not system drag-and-drop: the app under the pointer would accept the drop itself (paste text, move files). Nocchi runs its own drag.\n- The notch stays open during the drag (`isDraggingFace` in `holdsOpen`) and after the drop (the composer holds it open).\n- Esc, or dropping back on the notch, cancels; the face flies back. Reduce Motion: no flying, the face just appears at the pointer.\n- Without Accessibility: app and window title from `CGWindowList`, nothing inside the window. The label says so.\n- First feature that draws outside the notch: a window that follows the pointer, and the outline.\n\nReplaces PLAN.md's Deferred item \"Drag the face onto a window to start or point an agent at that app\".","sort_order":"a0","labels":["epic","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:00.916269Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-12168e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Nocchi MCP server: tools agents can call through the notch","description":"A `nocchi mcp` command that agents run as their MCP server (stdio). It passes calls to the running app over a local socket. You register it once with `claude mcp add nocchi -- nocchi mcp`. A call from inside a Herdr pane can say which agent made it, so the request shows on that agent's face.\n\n**Stages**\n1. `ask_user`: the agent asks a question, the notch opens with answer buttons, and the answer goes back to the agent.\n2. Read-only screen context: frontmost app and window, selected text, browser URL, open windows. The same capture as the face drag.\n3. Actions that ask first: focus a window, open a URL or file. Each call shows in the notch as a request you approve.\n4. Clicking and typing for the agent: probably never. Anything Nocchi exposes runs with its Accessibility permission, which any agent with the tool would then get, and Anthropic already offers computer use. If ever: per-session approval and a visible marker while it runs.","sort_order":"a1","labels":["epic","mcp"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:00.937684Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-7fac9b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"iPhone companion: the notch on the Lock Screen and in the Dynamic Island","description":"From PLAN.md M8. An iPhone app that mirrors the notch while you're away from the Mac.\n\n- The Mac app stays the source of truth.\n- Nothing leaves your devices unless you opt in.\n- Pairing happens once.","sort_order":"a2","labels":["epic","ios"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:00.95594Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-9ef931","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Face drag: drag sources, Nocchi's own drag, notch held open","description":"- Pressing on the focus card face, a chip face or the composer face starts a drag. The panel keeps receiving the pointer's movements outside its frame until release.\n- The face leaves the notch and follows the pointer in a small transparent window, looking curious.\n- `isDraggingFace` is part of `holdsOpen`.\n- Esc, or a drop back on the notch, cancels: the face flies back (no flying with Reduce Motion).\n- On release, hands the drop point and the drag source to context capture.","parent_id":"nchi-54ffe9","sort_order":"a3","labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.174793Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-dffc9d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Face drag: outline and label the window under the pointer","description":"- While dragging, find the window under the pointer with `AXUIElementCopyElementAtPosition`.\n- Draw a soft outline around it and a label such as \"Safari · webapp PR #12\".\n- Without Accessibility: the window's frame, app and title come from `CGWindowList`, and the label says only the window title can be read.\n- Never outlines Nocchi's own windows.","parent_id":"nchi-54ffe9","sort_order":"a4","labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.197316Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-252d64","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Face drag: capture context from the dropped-on window","description":"| Dropped on | Captured |\n|---|---|\n| A browser | Page URL and title, selected text |\n| An editor (Xcode, VS Code, Zed) | File path (`AXDocument`), selection, line |\n| Finder | Selected files, or the window's folder |\n| A terminal running a known agent | That agent: it becomes the target, not context |\n| Anything else | App, window title, selected text, focused field's value |\n\nAlso infer the project folder from a path when there is one. Screenshot of the window: opt-in with a modifier, needs Screen Recording.\n\nShared with the MCP read-only context tools (nchi-12168e).","parent_id":"nchi-54ffe9","sort_order":"a5","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.219864Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-045700","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Face drag: context chip in the composer and where the drop goes","description":"- After a drop, the composer opens with a removable context chip showing exactly what will be sent (e.g. \"Safari · github.com/nicbet/webapp/pull/12\").\n- New-chat face: a new agent starts with the context; the folder chip switches to the inferred project.\n- Agent face: the context goes with that agent's next message.\n- The context is added to the message text in a readable block, since Herdr's `agent.prompt` and `claude \"\u003cmessage\u003e\"` take text only.","parent_id":"nchi-54ffe9","sort_order":"a6","labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.242804Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-5f70ea","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP stage 1: `nocchi mcp` command with ask_user answered in the notch","description":"- `nocchi mcp`: a stdio MCP server that passes calls to the running app over a Unix socket. Errors clearly when Nocchi isn't running.\n- `ask_user(question, options?)`: the notch opens on the asking agent's face (matched via Herdr pane or Claude session) with answer buttons or a text field. The answer is returned to the agent. Timeouts and cancellation are reported back.\n- Setup docs: `claude mcp add nocchi -- nocchi mcp`.","parent_id":"nchi-12168e","sort_order":"a7","labels":["feature","mcp"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.263329Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-35941b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP stage 2: read-only screen context tools","description":"Tools: frontmost app and window, selected text, browser URL, open windows.\n\nReuses the face-drag context capture. Read-only, no approval per call, but a setting to turn them off, and the notch shows briefly when an agent reads the screen.","parent_id":"nchi-12168e","sort_order":"a8","labels":["feature","mcp"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.285064Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-9a3646","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP stage 3: actions that ask first (focus window, open URL or file)","description":"- Every call shows in the notch as a request on the agent's face, with Allow / Deny (and maybe \"allow for this session\").\n- No clicking or typing for the agent (see the epic).","parent_id":"nchi-12168e","sort_order":"a9","labels":["feature","mcp"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.30515Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-44656a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"iPhone: Live Activity and widget with the primary face and counts","description":"A Live Activity (Lock Screen and Dynamic Island) with Nocchi's face and mood for the primary agent and a count of the others, plus a Home and Lock Screen widget as the \"live tile\".","parent_id":"nchi-7fac9b","sort_order":"aA","labels":["feature","ios"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.325772Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-71a61a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"iPhone: choose the transport (APNs relay, Bonjour or CloudKit) and pairing","description":"The candidates:\n- ActivityKit push updates via APNs, which needs a small relay\n- the local network (Bonjour)\n- CloudKit\n\nPair once. Nothing leaves your devices without opting in.","parent_id":"nchi-7fac9b","sort_order":"aB","labels":["task","ios"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.349025Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-664ddb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"iPhone: Mac pushes AgentStore changes to the phone","description":"The Mac pushes status, step, done and needs-you to the phone.\n\n- Changes only, not full state.\n- Same \"done until seen\" rule as the notch.","parent_id":"nchi-7fac9b","sort_order":"aC","labels":["feature","ios"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.369863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-c27dc6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"iPhone: tap a waiting agent to see what it's asking","description":"Tapping a waiting agent shows its question. Answering from the phone is a stretch goal.","parent_id":"nchi-7fac9b","sort_order":"aD","labels":["feature","ios"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.389275Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-7bb337","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"A newly started agent becomes the main face","description":"After a new chat (or a folder drop) starts an agent, it shows up among the chips, because `AgentAction.start` doesn't return which agent it created.\n\nHave Herdr's start report the pane, so the new agent can be made the main face (`store.select`).\n\nFor the terminal-tab fallback, match the new Claude session by its folder and start time instead.","sort_order":"aE","labels":["feature","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.409558Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-48617b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Check a real Herdr start with a first message in a throwaway session","description":"The new-chat flow (`workspace.create` → `agent.start` → `agent.prompt`, retrying `agent_not_ready`) has only run against the mock adapter.\n\nAdd an integration test in an isolated `nocchi-it-*` Herdr session that starts Claude with a one-line prompt and sees it start working.\n\nUses the user's Claude account (a tiny prompt), so ask before running it.","sort_order":"aF","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.427982Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-020665","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Try the top bar and new chat on screen (Home, Chat, folder menu, Choose…, gear)","description":"Checked only in offscreen snapshots so far. Needs clicks in the notch, so do it with the user.\n\nCheck:\n- the SwiftUI folder `Menu` opens inside the non-activating panel\n- Choose… brings up the folder picker and the chat stays open meanwhile\n- the gear's menu appears at the pointer\n- the fallback terminal tab works with Herdr turned off\n- icons sit comfortably in the 24 pt strip on an external display","sort_order":"aG","labels":["task","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.447243Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-eaa8de","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Performance budget check in Instruments","description":"From PLAN.md M7. Measure idle CPU, energy impact and wake-ups.\n\nLevers if needed:\n- a lower display-link rate for calm moods\n- stopping the link while the pointer and face are still","sort_order":"aH","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.469962Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-c740b3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Showcase recorder (Debug ▸ Record Showcase…)","description":"From PLAN.md M7.\n\n**What it records:** a scripted demo. A mock scenario plus a timeline of notch actions: greeting, peeks, alert, hover, composer, folder drop. A fake pointer drives it, also steers the gaze, and is drawn as a cursor.\n\n**How:**\n- ScreenCaptureKit's `SCRecordingOutput`, cropped to the notch, at Retina 60 fps, on a neutral backdrop window\n- writes a `.mov` to the Desktop\n- needs Screen Recording permission for Nocchi, asked once\n- real-time capture on purpose: offscreen `ImageRenderer` frames can't show SwiftUI animations","sort_order":"aI","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.489346Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-bf8921","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Slim PLAN.md down to decisions and architecture; point to xpo","description":"Now that open work lives in xpo:\n- remove PLAN.md's open checklist items and the Deferred section\n- keep the decision table, architecture, Herdr protocol notes, and the milestone history\n- add a pointer to the xpo board","sort_order":"aJ","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:40:34.507829Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
