{"id":"nchi-266732","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e83efbbb-5be9-4e7b-964b-b0a4f9959c5b","text":"Implemented: `scripts/create-signing-cert.sh` (ported from colorsip, identity `${SIGNING_IDENTITY:-Local App Signing}`, no xcconfig), identity check in `bundle.sh` with ad hoc fallback, `make signing-cert` / `make reset-permissions`, and a README note. The ad hoc hint goes to stderr because `dev.sh` reads the app path from the last stdout line. The Makefile help column is widened for the longer target names.\n\nVerified: the fallback path signs ad hoc and prints the hint. Not yet verified: the identity path, which needs `make signing-cert` (keychain write and password prompt), so the user has to run it."},"created_at":"2026-10-16T08:15:55.93025Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.301 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"nchi-266732","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-71114aab-d080-4f09-94b5-6e92a9c1a18b","text":"Identity path verified after the user ran `make signing-cert`. The designated requirement is `identifier \"com.github.nicbet.nocchi\" and certificate leaf = H\"9348718a…\"`. It is identical after a rebuild and no longer depends on the cdhash."},"created_at":"2026-10-16T08:18:30.36489Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.301 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
