{"id":"nchi-d320c5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ea31b969-689f-4554-9b72-1ae9bcf9a9a3","text":"Implemented per spec; `swift test` passes (147 tests, 7 new).\n\n- NocchiCore: `AgentHost { pid, windowHints }`, `AgentInfo.host` (init param, default nil).\n- Claude: tracker sets `host` = (terminal pid, [latest ai-title, folder]) when the pid's terminal is known; adapter caches titles per session for 5 s.\n- Herdr: `HerdrTracker.setHost(_:)` plus host refresh on title / tab rename / pane updates; `HerdrAdapter(locatesHost:)` (default false) looks up the preferred Herdr client terminal on each reconcile.\n- NocchiTerminals: `WindowRaiser.windowID(in:matching:)` — shared candidate collection + `bestCandidate` with `raise`, 0.25 s AX messaging timeout, `_AXUIElementGetWindow`, no actions.\n- Docs: README Development + PLAN M6.\n\nNot in the spec: `paneUpdated` now also records the pane's workspace, so hints (and Nocchi's own \"open\") follow an agent that moves to another workspace. AgentSpaces needs `HerdrAdapter(socketPath: …, locatesHost: true)` to get Herdr hosts. `windowID` not checked live (needs an Accessibility-trusted process)."},"created_at":"2026-10-16T12:18:59.788144Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.301 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
